et="_blank" class="sc-iRgEWu hHENWX">official Twitter account</a>, the Paris Police Prefecture said the fire was the product of a “technical incident” involving a “truck with fireworks”.</p><p>It also said the fire did not occur at the tower itself, but on the neighbouring Jena Bridge,</p><div class="sc-iKFaHN fAfkdY"><div id="adspot-tablet-banner-2-below"></div><div id="adspot-mobile-mobile-2-above"></div><small class="sc-gKkgUA jQWpfi _0b53bae146db0b62 _309631c94c78212c" style="--text-color:var(--color-text-secondary)">Advertisement</small></div><p>Police advised the public to avoid the area.</p><p>Video and photos taken by witnesses show what appear to be flames near the foot of the monument and black smoke clouds partially obscuring the tower.</p><p>The images initially sparked panic on social media in the wake of news a truck ploughed through a crowd in Nice amid Bastille Day celebrations, killing up to 60 people.</p><div class="sc-kjWMno hQNvCp"><div class="OB-REACT-WRAPPER"><div class="OUTBRAIN" data-src="https://nine.com.au/world-news/eiffel-tower-blaze-a-technical-incident-involving-a-truck-with-fireworks-police-say-20160715-p5ujwj.html" data-widget-id="AR_5"></div></div></div><strong>READ MORE:<!-- --> </strong><a href="/world-news/reports-of-injuries-after-vehicle-crashes-into-crowd-during-bastille-day-celebrations-in-nice-france-20160716-p5ujw4.html" class="sc-iRgEWu hHENWX">At least 30 dead after truck slams into crowd during Bastille Day celebrations in Nice</a></div></div><footer><div class="sc-jWiywy gKFWdE"><ul data-ui-testid="footer-tags" class="sc-bybPKr gSwTnX"><li><a class="sc-czxEME graVLC _2b8391ba0eafd919 _4e4903bbc1d6afc3 c1611628a5f010bc _24b4f09f725e52fa" href="/topic/france-9ug" style="--component-style-link-color:var(--color-neutral-600);--component-style-link-color-active:var(--color-neutral-800);--component-style-link-color-hover:var(--color-neutral-700)">France</a></li></ul></div></footer><section class="sc-hREPRl" data-contentunit-pu